    {
      "documentId": "74ef287e-7d95-42b1-a7de-878aa7f6dfdd",
      "value": "The evolutionary strategy used by cicadas of the genus Magicicada make use of prime numbers.",
      "start": 29,
      "end": 121,
      "similarity": 0.17073945175513378,
      "facetSimilarities": []
    },
    {
      "documentId": "74ef287e-7d95-42b1-a7de-878aa7f6dfdd",
      "value": "These insects spend most of their lives as grubs underground.",
      "start": 122,
      "end": 183,
      "similarity": 0.07901359849811879,
      "facetSimilarities": []
    },
    {
      "documentId": "74ef287e-7d95-42b1-a7de-878aa7f6dfdd",
      "value": "They only pupate and then emerge from their burrows after 7, 13 or 17 years, at which point they fly about, breed, and then die after a few weeks at most.",
      "start": 184,
      "end": 338,
      "similarity": 0.00429612684985542,
      "facetSimilarities": []
    },
    {
      "documentId": "74ef287e-7d95-42b1-a7de-878aa7f6dfdd",
      "value": "The logic for this is believed to be that the prime number intervals between emergences make it very difficult for predators to evolve that could specialize as predators on Magicicadas.",
      "start": 339,
      "end": 524,
      "similarity": 0.012780024670114513,
      "facetSimilarities": []
    },
    {
      "documentId": "74ef287e-7d95-42b1-a7de-878aa7f6dfdd",
      "value": "If Magicicadas appeared at a non-prime number intervals, say every 12 years, then predators appearing every 2, 3, 4, 6, or 12 years would be sure to meet them.",
      "start": 525,
      "end": 684,
      "similarity": 0.07370773732965746,
      "facetSimilarities": []
    },
    {
      "documentId": "74ef287e-7d95-42b1-a7de-878aa7f6dfdd",
      "value": "Over a 200-year period, average predator populations during hypothetical outbreaks of 14- and 15-year cicadas would be up to 2% higher than during outbreaks of 13- and 17-year cicadas.",
      "start": 685,
      "end": 869,
      "similarity": -0.05005835462911124,
      "facetSimilarities": []
    },
    {
      "documentId": "74ef287e-7d95-42b1-a7de-878aa7f6dfdd",
      "value": "Though small, this advantage appears to have been enough to drive natural selection in favour of a prime-numbered life-cycle for these insects.",
