      "documentId": "ba674cb4-c4c5-421e-b592-1556ba0797c0",
      "value": "Chloroplasts' main role is to conduct photosynthesis, where the photosynthetic pigment chlorophyll captures the energy from sunlight and converts it and stores it in the energy-storage molecules ATP and NADPH while freeing oxygen from water.",
      "start": 28,
      "end": 269,
